er":{"code":"CDMS","name":"Legacy CDMS","id":"092d6e0881874968859b972d39a888dc"},"onlyAbstract":false,"sensitiveInformation":2,"abstract":"The design and fabrication of a dual spin gas bearing reaction wheel are discussed. Numerical analyses, data, and conclusions from performance tests are reported. The unique feature of the reaction wheel is the dual gas bearing concept in which two sets of self-acting hydrodynamic bearing are used to obtain stictionless operation and low noise around zero speed and to accommodate the momentum range from plus 6.8 N-m-s to minus 6.8 N-m-s with the potential for long life inherent in gas bearings.","isLessonsLearned":false,"disseminated":"DOCUMENT_AND_METADATA","publications":[{"submissionId":19740012956,"id":"a61588ef19ec450681a71d99fec9aba4","publicationDate":"1973-11-01T00:00:00.0000000+00:00"}],"status":"CURATED","related":[],"downloads":[{"draft":false,"mimetype":"application/pdf","name":"19740012956.pdf","type":"STI","links":{"original":"/api/citations/19740012956/downloads/19740012956.pdf","pdf":"/api/citations/19740012956/downloads/19740012956.pdf","fulltext":"/api/citations/19740012956/downloads/19740012956.txt"}}],"downloadsAvailable":true,"index":"submissions-2026-11-12-06-24"},{"_meta":{"score":84.76837},"copyright":{"thirdPartyPermissionsProduced":false,"disclosedToPublic":false,"containsIndication":false,"publisherPermissionOrRightsToDistribute":false,"belongsToUsGov":false,"determinationType":"PUBLIC_USE_PERMITTED","thirdPartyContentCondition":"NOT_SET","belongsToContractor":false,"disclosedInvention":false,"submissionId":20090029851,"containsThirdPartyMaterial":false,"belongsToPublisher":false,"id":"0de94f2f9ccb467e8b3b93a5261406cf","belongsToAuthors":false},"subjectCategories":["Man/System Technology And Life Support"],"exportControl":{"isExportControl":"NO","submissionId":20090029851,"ear":"NO","id":"11c90264851c4bf787954cde2ae7b185","itar":"NO"},"distributionDate":"2019-07-12T00:00:00.0000000+00:00","otherReportNumbers":["JSC-CN-18714","Report Number: JSC-CN-18714"],"fundingNumbers":[{"number":"NNX08AY09G","submissionId":20090029851,"id":"c976984c14e344c0a7ccca4b2da3584b","type":"CONTRACT_GRANT"}],"title":"Psychomotor Vigilance Self Test on ISS (Reaction Self Test on Expeditions 21 and 22)","stiType":"PRESENTATION","distribution":"PUBLIC","submittedDate":"2013-08-24T18:49:00.0000000+00:00","authorAffiliations":[{"sequence":0,"submissionId":20090029851,"meta":{"author":{"name":"Dinges, David F."},"organization":{"name":"Pennsylvania Univ. Medical Center","location":"Philadelphia, PA, United States"}},"id":"c7ad3469834947b4b745cd894e491be8"},{"sequence":1,"submissionId":20090029851,"meta":{"author":{"name":"Mollicone, Daniel"},"organization":{"name":"Pulsar Informatics","location":"Norfolk, VA, United States"}},"id":"2f1cbbf5323844b2ab0995b5f00863dd"},{"sequence":2,"submissionId":20090029851,"meta":{"author":{"name":"Ecker, Adrian"},"organization":{"name":"Pennsylvania Univ. Medical Center","location":"Philadelphia, PA, United States"}},"id":"0ade9b5a8e104ea09e62643b41c6d303"}],"stiTypeDetails":"Presentation","technicalReviewType":"TECHNICAL_REVIEW_TYPE_NONE","modified":"2025-08-31T18:39:21.7150190+00:00","id":20090029851,"legacyMeta":{"__type":"LegacyMetaIndex, StrivesApi.ServiceModel","accessionNumber":""},"created":"2013-08-24T18:49:00.0000000+00:00","center":{"code":"JSC","name":"Johnson Space Center","id":"dd46994b91a94cb2a2722617cbbadc55"},"onlyAbstract":false,"sensitiveInformation":2,"abstract":"The experiment addresses the following high-priority NASA Risk Gaps in the Behavioral Health and Performance (BHP) area: 1) Identify brief, valid objective measures of changes in cognitive functions during spaceflight that astronauts can use with minimal burden. 2) Find a practical objective aid for astronauts to quickly identify and manage the effects of fatigue (from sleep loss, circadian disruptions, workload and other factors) on their performance during space flight.","isLessonsLearned":false,"disseminated":"DOCUMENT_AND_METADATA","meetings":[{"submissionId":20090029851,"name":"NASA Johnson Space Center","location":"Houston, TX, United States","id":"615558209d8a44e582d99f70ecc0eef1"},{"country":"United States","submissionId":20090029851,"endDate":"2009-09-03T00:00:00.0000000+00:00","sponsors":[{"meta":{"organization":{"name":"NASA Johnson Space Center","location":"Houston, TX, United States"}},"meetingId":"caabb747fb044775870cc1816d445df8","id":"770a8a04610c4b0db2f83438dba42f70"}],"name":"Increment 21/22 Science Symposium","location":"Houston, TX","id":"caabb747fb044775870cc1816d445df8","startDate":"2009-09-02T00:00:00.0000000+00:00"}],"publications":[{"submissionId":20090029851,"id":"74a64ccfdcab48f29d1785ed050b963b","publicationDate":"2009-01-01T00:00:00.0000000+00:00"}],"status":"CURATED","related":[],"downloads":[{"draft":false,"mimetype":"application/pdf","name":"20090029851.pdf","type":"STI","links":{"original":"/api/citations/20090029851/downloads/20090029851.pdf","pdf":"/api/citations/20090029851/downloads/20090029851.pdf","fulltext":"/api/citations/20090029851/downloads/20090029851.txt"}}],"downloadsAvailable":true,"index":"submissions-2026-11-12-06-24"},{"_meta":{"score":81.711},"copyright":{"thirdPartyPermissionsProduced":false,"disclosedToPublic":false,"containsIndication":false,"publisherPermissionOrRightsToDistribute":false,"belongsToUsGov":false,"determinationType":"GOV_PUBLIC_USE_PERMITTED","thirdPartyContentCondition":"NOT_SET","belongsToContractor":false,"disclosedInvention":false,"submissionId":20150018353,"containsThirdPartyMaterial":false,"belongsToPublisher":false,"id":"a64c605c6eed49339b43240896456ebb","belongsToAuthors":false},"subjectCategories":["Man/System Technology And Life Support"],"keywords":["Technology Portfolio System","Technology Portfolio System","Technology Portfolio System"],"exportControl":{"isExportControl":"NO","submissionId":20150018353,"ear":"NO","id":"accd6781292747a488be52613d8137ae","itar":"NO"},"distributionDate":"2019-07-11T00:00:00.0000000+00:00","otherReportNumbers":["KSC-E-DAA-TN25611","Report Number: KSC-E-DAA-TN25611"],"title":"Self-Cleaning Boudouard Reactor for Full Oxygen Recovery from CO2 Project","stiType":"OTHER","distribution":"PUBLIC","submittedDate":"2015-09-24T13:49:08.3770000+00:00","authorAffiliations":[{"sequence":0,"submissionId":20150018353,"meta":{"author":{"name":"Zeitlin, Nancy"},"organization":{"name":"NASA Kennedy Space Center","location":"Cocoa Beach, FL United States"}},"id":"ff2c8b69e5914f4a95a87b8a82c4b750"},{"sequence":1,"submissionId":20150018353,"meta":{"author":{"name":"Muscatello, Anthony"},"organization":{"name":"NASA Kennedy Space Center","location":"Cocoa Beach, FL United States"}},"id":"09b63c0af5c441caa2018da7657165fb"}],"stiTypeDetails":"Other","technicalReviewType":"TECHNICAL_REVIEW_TYPE_NONE","modified":"2025-08-31T18:39:21.7150190+00:00","id":20150018353,"legacyMeta":{"__type":"LegacyMetaIndex, StrivesApi.ServiceModel","accessionNumber":""},"created":"2015-09-24T13:49:08.3770000+00:00","center":{"code":"KSC","name":"Kennedy Space Center","id":"a74d241e0e974719b03cb45cbace6b20"},"onlyAbstract":false,"sensitiveInformation":2,"abstract":"Oxygen recovery from respiratory CO2 is an important aspect of human spaceflight. Methods exist to sequester the CO2, but production of oxygen needs further development. The current ISS Carbon Dioxide Reduction System (CRS) uses the Sabatier reaction to produce water (and ultimately breathing air). Oxygen recovery is limited to 50% because half of the hydrogen used in the Sabatier reactor is lost as methane, which is vented overboard. The Bosch reaction is the only real alternative to the Sabatier reaction, but in the last reaction in the cycle (Boudouard) the resulting carbon buildup will eventually foul the nickel or iron catalyst, reducing reactor life and increasing consumables. To minimize this fouling, find a use for this waste product, and increase efficiency, we propose testing various self-cleaning catalyst designs in an existing MSFC Boudouard reaction test bed and to determine which one is the most reliable in conversion and lack of fouling. Challenges include mechanical reliability of the cleaning method and maintaining high conversion efficiency with lower catalyst surface area. The above chemical reactions are well understood, but planned implementations are novel (TRL 2) and haven't been investigated at any level.","isLessonsLearned":false,"disseminated":"DOCUMENT_AND_METADATA","publications":[{"submissionId":20150018353,"id":"00fe33583d014623b23fc2a70301c23c","publicationDate":"2015-08-07T00:00:00.0000000+00:00"}],"status":"CURATED","related":[{"disseminated":"DOCUMENT_AND_METADATA","id":20160008967,"type":"SEE_ALSO","title":"Self-Cleaning Boudouard Reactor for Full Oxygen Recovery from Carbon Dioxide","stiType":"CONFERENCE_PAPER","distribution":"PUBLIC","status":"CURATED"},{"disseminated":"DOCUMENT_AND_METADATA","id":20160008967,"type":"SEE_ALSO","title":"Self-Cleaning Boudouard Reactor for Full Oxygen Recovery from Carbon Dioxide","stiType":"CONFERENCE_PAPER","distribution":"PUBLIC","status":"CURATED"}],"downloads":[{"draft":false,"mimetype":"application/pdf","name":"20150018353.pdf","type":"STI","links":{"original":"/api/citations/20150018353/downloads/20150018353.pdf","pdf":"/api/citations/20150018353/downloads/20150018353.pdf","fulltext":"/api/citations/20150018353/downloads/20150018353.txt"}}],"downloadsAvailable":true,"index":"submissions-2026-11-12-06-24"},{"_meta":{"score":74.70508},"copyright":{"thirdPartyPermissionsProduced":false,"disclosedToPublic":false,"containsIndication":false,"publisherPermissionOrRightsToDistribute":false,"belongsToUsGov":false,"determinationType":"OTHER","thirdPartyContentCondition":"NOT_SET","belongsToContractor":false,"disclosedInvention":false,"submissionId":19930045951,"containsThirdPartyMaterial":false,"belongsToPublisher":false,"id":"182c74054722450e9e7be9d6a37f1a4a","belongsToAuthors":false},"subjectCategories":["Composite Materials"],"exportControl":{"isExportControl":"NO","submissionId":19930045951,"ear":"NO","id":"dce79422d3e14f55959dfe4d6593eda7","itar":"NO"},"distributionDate":"2011-08-19T00:00:00.0000000+00:00","otherReportNumbers":["ISSN: 0022-2461"],"title":"Sliding wear of self-mated Al2O3-SiC whisker-reinforced composites at 23-1200 C","stiType":"REPRINT","distribution":"PUBLIC","submittedDate":"2013-08-16T00:42:00.0000000+00:00","authorAffiliations":[{"sequence":0,"submissionId":19930045951,"meta":{"author":{"name":"Farmer, S. C."},"organization":{"name":"NASA Lewis Research Center","location":"Cleveland, OH, United States"}},"id":"8a2683ac7a7549eebe46ea10c6d06324"},{"sequence":1,"submissionId":19930045951,"meta":{"author":{"name":"Dellacorte, C."},"organization":{"name":"NASA Lewis Research Center","location":"Cleveland, OH, United States"}},"id":"7832f7f35b524cd18f05c704a44970a0"},{"sequence":2,"submissionId":19930045951,"meta":{"author":{"name":"Book, P. O."},"organization":{"name":"Cleveland State Univ.; NASA, Lewis Research Center","location":"OH, United States"}},"id":"098ea55ddb7043a5afd02ccad47b4e47"}],"stiTypeDetails":"Reprint (Version printed in journal)","technicalReviewType":"TECHNICAL_REVIEW_TYPE_NONE","modified":"2025-08-31T18:39:21.7150190+00:00","id":19930045951,"sourceIdentifiers":[{"number":"doi:10.1007/BF01191945","submissionId":19930045951,"id":"bd8ec7d3994847f0896797a61aaa3f3e","type":"DOI"},{"submissionId":19930045951,"id":"9dc2275e27fd4abfb7a1b48d06e1c6a6","descriptor":"doi:10.1007/BF01191945"}],"legacyMeta":{"__type":"LegacyMetaIndex, StrivesApi.ServiceModel","accessionNumber":"93A29948"},"created":"2013-08-16T00:42:00.0000000+00:00","center":{"code":"CDMS","name":"Legacy CDMS","id":"092d6e0881874968859b972d39a888dc"},"onlyAbstract":false,"sensitiveInformation":2,"abstract":"Microstructural changes occurring during sliding wear of self-mated Al2O3 SiC whisker-reinforced composites were studied using optical, scanning electron microscopy and transmission electron microscopy. Pin-on-disc specimens were slid in air at 2.7 m/s sliding velocity under a 26.5 N load for 1 h. Wear tests were conducted at 23, 600, 800 and 1200 C. Mild wear with a wear factor of 2.4 x 10 exp -7 - 1.5 x 10 exp -6 cu mm /N per m was experienced at all test temperatures. The composite showed evidence of wear by fatigue mechanisms at 800 C and below. Tribochemical reaction (SiC oxidation and reaction of SiO2 and Al2O3) leads to intergranular failure at 1200 C. Distinct microstructural differences existing at each test temperature are reported.","isLessonsLearned":false,"disseminated":"METADATA_ONLY","publications":[{"volume":"28","submissionId":19930045951,"issue":"5","issn":"0022-2461","id":"cf47937fd48a4d36ae72bed189b8eb10","publicationName":"Journal of Materials Science","publicationDate":"1993-03-01T00:00:00.0000000+00:00"}],"status":"CURATED","related":[],"downloads":[],"downloadsAvailable":false,"index":"submissions-2026-11-12-06-24"},{"_meta":{"score":74.616745},"copyright":{"thirdPartyPermissionsProduced":false,"disclosedToPublic":false,"containsIndication":false,"publisherPermissionOrRightsToDistribute":false,"belongsToUsGov":false,"determinationType":"GOV_PUBLIC_USE_PERMITTED","thirdPartyContentCondition":"NOT_SET","belongsToContractor":false,"disclosedInvention":false,"submissionId":19910017907,"containsThirdPartyMaterial":false,"belongsToPublisher":false,"id":"314d89fdf4cf4bb7ae8c8fb24b041f3f","belongsToAuthors":false},"subjectCategories":["Chemistry And Materials (General)"],"exportControl":{"isExportControl":"NO","submissionId":19910017907,"ear":"NO","id":"e59361e165e74899a71a2f39175bcc26","itar":"NO"},"distributionDate":"2019-06-25T00:00:00.0000000+00:00","otherReportNumbers":["NAS 1.15:104490","E-6344","NASA-TM-104490","Report Number: NAS 1.15:104490","Report Number: E-6344","Report Number: NASA-TM-104490"],"fundingNumbers":[{"number":"RTOP 505-63-10","submissionId":19910017907,"id":"63c1c45325c0426aa3bcfb3c3df0ab5e","type":"PROJECT"}],"title":"Sliding wear of self-mated Al2O3-SiC whisker reinforced composites at 23-1200 C","stiType":"TECHNICAL_MEMORANDUM","distribution":"PUBLIC","submittedDate":"2013-09-06T14:42:00.0000000+00:00","authorAffiliations":[{"sequence":0,"submissionId":19910017907,"meta":{"author":{"name":"Farmer, Serene C."},"organization":{"name":"NASA Lewis Research Center","location":"Cleveland, OH., United States"}},"id":"e5ae8a1f78724ed98d779f601d3210fd"},{"sequence":1,"submissionId":19910017907,"meta":{"author":{"name":"Book, Patricia O."},"organization":{"name":"Cleveland State Univ.","location":"OH., United States"}},"id":"2a14536072d949b2b4ac49d1393884db"},{"sequence":2,"submissionId":19910017907,"meta":{"author":{"name":"Dellacorte, Christopher"},"organization":{"name":"NASA Lewis Research Center","location":"Cleveland, OH, United States"}},"id":"6e520378d1d543c7a5ea2ea14c99d01a"}],"stiTypeDetails":"Technical Memorandum (TM)","technicalReviewType":"TECHNICAL_REVIEW_TYPE_NONE","modified":"2025-08-31T18:39:21.7150190+00:00","id":19910017907,"legacyMeta":{"__type":"LegacyMetaIndex, StrivesApi.ServiceModel","accessionNumber":"91N27221"},"created":"2013-09-06T14:42:00.0000000+00:00","center":{"code":"CDMS","name":"Legacy CDMS","id":"092d6e0881874968859b972d39a888dc"},"onlyAbstract":false,"sensitiveInformation":2,"abstract":"Microstructural changes occurring during sliding wear of self-mated Al2O3-SiC whisker reinforced composites were studied using optical, scanning electron microscopy, and transmission electron microscopy. Pin-on-disk specimens were slid in air at 2.7 m/sec sliding velocity under a 26.5 N load for 1 hr. Wear tests were conducted at 23, 600, 800, and 1200 C. Mild wear with a wear factor of 2.4 times 10(exp -7) to 1.5 times 10(exp -6) cu mm/Nm was experienced at all test temperatures. The composite shows evidence of wear by fatigue mechanisms at 800 C and below. Tribochemical reaction (SiC oxidation and reaction of SiO2 and Al2O3) leads to intergranular failure at 1200 C. Distinct microstructural differences existing at each test temperature are reported.","isLessonsLearned":false,"disseminated":"DOCUMENT_AND_METADATA","publications":[{"submissionId":19910017907,"id":"bc821c1eb8004f089c57fcc96ccc1d3f","publicationDate":"1991-07-01T00:00:00.0000000+00:00"}],"status":"CURATED","related":[],"downloads":[{"draft":false,"mimetype":"application/pdf","name":"19910017907.pdf","type":"STI","links":{"original":"/api/citations/19910017907/downloads/19910017907.pdf","pdf":"/api/citations/19910017907/downloads/19910017907.pdf","fulltext":"/api/citations/19910017907/downloads/19910017907.txt"}}],"downloadsAvailable":true,"index":"submissions-2026-11-12-06-24"},{"_meta":{"score":71.98994},"copyright":{"thirdPartyPermissionsProduced":false,"disclosedToPublic":false,"containsIndication":false,"publisherPermissionOrRightsToDistribute":false,"belongsToUsGov":false,"determinationType":"OTHER","thirdPartyContentCondition":"NOT_SET","belongsToContractor":false,"disclosedInvention":false,"submissionId":19880054115,"containsThirdPartyMaterial":false,"belongsToPublisher":false,"id":"a188a432d7294b029235a984d3b64e79","belongsToAuthors":false},"subjectCategories":["Spacecraft Design, Testing And Performance"],"exportControl":{"isExportControl":"NO","submissionId":19880054115,"ear":"NO","id":"ba3b57bd04b742d48c3c4566bea8eddc","itar":"NO"},"distributionDate":"2019-07-12T00:00:00.0000000+00:00","fundingNumbers":[{"number":"NAS8-35257","submissionId":19880054115,"id":"46005e0e2e594bca98414896f655bcd0","type":"CONTRACT_GRANT"}],"title":"Self-contained space qualifiable optical contamination monitor","stiType":"CONFERENCE_PAPER","distribution":"PUBLIC","submittedDate":"2013-08-13T15:54:00.0000000+00:00","authorAffiliations":[{"sequence":0,"submissionId":19880054115,"meta":{"author":{"name":"Jarratt, R. V., Jr."},"organization":{"name":"Acton Research Corp.","location":"MA, United States"}},"id":"3a1